{
  "id": "how_to_calculate_the_density_of_slurries__formula_",
  "title": "How to Calculate the Density of Slurries: Formula and Examples",
  "description": "Calculate the density of slurries using the standard formula. A slurry is a mixture of a solid and a liquid. Input the concentration of solids by weight, density of solids, and density of liquid to determine the slurry density.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "Slurry Density Calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "cw",
          "label": "Concentration of Solids by Weight (cw)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "%",
          "defaultValue": 30
        },
        {
          "id": "rho_s",
          "label": "Density of Solids (ρs)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 2500
        },
        {
          "id": "rho_l",
          "label": "Density of Liquid (ρl)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "rho_m",
          "label": "Density of Slurry (ρm)",
          "formula": "100 / (inputs.cw / inputs.rho_s + (100 - inputs.cw) / inputs.rho_l)",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "sg",
          "label": "Specific Gravity (SG)",
          "formula": "(100 / (inputs.cw / inputs.rho_s + (100 - inputs.cw) / inputs.rho_l)) / 1000",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Formula\n\n**ρm = 100 / (cw / ρs + (100 - cw) / ρl)**\n\nWhere:\n- **ρm** = density of slurry (kg/m³)\n- **cw** = concentration of solids by weight in the slurry (%)\n- **ρs** = density of the solids (kg/m³)\n- **ρl** = density of liquid without solids (kg/m³)\n\n## Example\n\nFor a slurry with:\n- Density of solids: 2500 kg/m³\n- Density of liquid: 1000 kg/m³\n- Weight concentration of solids: 30%\n\nThe slurry density = 100 / ((30) / (2500) + (70) / (1000)) = **1220 kg/m³**"
    },
    {
